// ---- queries/v1/cognition/spaceParticipantPresence.memql ----

// spaceParticipantPresence - Presence snapshots for a space
// =========================================================
//
// Returns every v1:cognition:participant:presence row for a space.
// The SPA keys these latest-wins by participantId (useParticipantPresence
// + SpaceSubscriptionContext) to drive the presence panel's per-agent
// status pill + the chat activity indicator. Space-scoped, same gating
// shape as spaceParticipants (the calling path verifies the caller
// is a space participant).

@description("Presence snapshots for every participant in a space (UI state: thinking / responding / waiting / ...). Space-scoped; the SPA dedupes latest-wins by participantId.")
@unbounded("presence rows for a space -- bounded by space participants, consumed whole")
query presence spaceParticipantPresence {
  args {
    partitionId  string!
  }
  filter  partitionId==args.partitionId
  shape   presenceFull
}

// ---- queries/v1/cognition/activeDailySpacesForUser.memql ----

// activeDailySpacesForUser - Daily-rollover sweep helper
// ======================================================
//
// Returns the still-active (not yet rolled-over) daily spaces owned by
// the given user. Used ONLY by the dailyspace integration's rollover
// sweep (integrations/dailyspace, memql#1384): the hourly cron walks
// every active user, ensures today's daily exists, then sweeps any
// active daily whose dailyDateKey is before the user's local today --
// ending participants, clearing presence, deleting the LiveKit room,
// and archiving/saving the space per preferences.dailySpaceRolloverAction.
//
// statusIsActive + isActiveRecord are what make the sweep
// idempotent at the query level: once a daily is rolled over (status
// archived/saved, active=false) it drops out of this result set, so a
// re-run -- on this replica or a concurrent one -- finds nothing to do.
//
// `@public` marks this query as intentionally not caller-scoped: it is
// invoked exclusively under the system:dailyspaceAutomation actor with
// a server-supplied userId from activeUsers (never caller input),
// mirroring queryAllArchivedSpacesAcrossUsers' cron-sweep precedent.

